  "id": "generalized-other",
  "term": "generalized other",
  "definition": "In this context, the generalized other means a person’s broad expectation of how other people typically react to them across everyday situations, rather than in relation to one specific person. It reflects a general self-with-others pattern that summarizes basic interpersonal tendencies.",
